<title>INDIA: Indian silver ends sharply up on firm world trend.</title>
<headline>Indian silver ends sharply up on firm world trend.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>** Silver (.999) closes 175 rupees higher at 7,025 rupees per kg on speculative support triggered by a firm world trend.</p>
<p>** Gold 24 carat ends 40 rupees up at 4,800 rupees per 10 grammes on seasonal buying and a rally in the world market.</p>
<p>** Prices of a gold biscuits (116.50 grammes) closes 400 rupees higher at 56,100 rupees per piece against the previous close of 55,700 rupees.</p>
<p>-- </p>
